  "note": "PROMOTION RULE, learned the hard way: a mutant counts as CAUGHT only when the criterion fails on its OWN assertion. A failure of INCONCLUSIVE — a click that never dispatched, a restart that was refused — also drops the score, and reads as detection while proving nothing. Check the failure text, never just the number. PROMOTION PROCEDURE: a zero-point criterion cannot be mutation-tested directly, because mutation-test.mjs detects a defect as a score DROP and zero minus zero is no change — every mutant 'survives' by construction. Prove a criterion against a scored copy instead: regenerate grader/.candidates/ecom-contention-scored.json (same steps, 1 point each), run mutation-test.mjs against THAT, and promote here only what was CAUGHT. EVERY CRITERION SCORES ZERO ON PURPOSE. A criterion here is a claim that concurrent customers can break an application, and that claim is not proven until this suite has actually caught a defect. The chat track's contention criteria were withheld for the same reason and are still withheld, because the failure they predicted never appeared. Promote a criterion to real points only when grader/mutation-test.mjs shows it CAUGHT its mutant in grader/mutations/<backend>-ecom-l1.json AND it passes against the unmutated reference build. Record which mutant proved it in `provenBy` when promoting. Until then these run, and their results are reported, but they cannot move a score in either direction.",
